<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fētĭdus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">faet-, foet-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		feteo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i>that has an ill smell</i>, <i>stinking</i>, <i>fetid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anima fetida,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 3, 3, 13</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum isto ore fetido teterrimam nobis popinam
					inhalasses,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 6, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pisces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 4, 2, 33</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dejectiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 3,
					2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Fig., <i>foul</i>, <i>disgusting</i>:
			libido, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2,
			245.—Of heresy (<i>sup.</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fetidissimus fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 7, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
